## Context

Child of 0700 (tracker 2070). After the end-to-end run 2071, decide from measured band width and recall whether a second scorer (another vendor, own calibrated cut) and a referee on the band (local model with llguidance and positive and negative few-shots, or a third API vendor) are worth their cost. The design if adopted is in section 2.4 of `docs/rel-pipeline-redesign-2026-10-10.md`; price lines are in its section 9.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Band width and recall at the cut quoted from 2071, by act and language.
- [ ] Price of the second scorer and of the referee derived for the band only, not for the whole pool.
- [ ] A recommendation with its evidence; the author's decision logged. If adopted, a build ticket is filed with the price as its ceiling; if not, the reason is recorded for the methods section of the review.
